# IndiGo Airline Business Analytics

## Project Objective
The objective of this project is to analyze IndiGo Airlines’ operational and financial
performance using business analytics techniques and derive actionable insights to
improve route profitability and operational efficiency.

import pandas as pd
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt

plt.style.use("default")

df = pd.read_csv("../data/IndiGo_Airline_Operations_Data.csv")
df.head()

df.info()
df.describe()

route_profit = df.groupby("Route")["Operating_Profit_INR"].sum().sort_values(ascending=False)

route_profit.plot(kind="bar", figsize=(10,5))
plt.title("Route-wise Operating Profit")
plt.xlabel("Route")
plt.ylabel("Operating Profit (INR)")
plt.show()

plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))
plt.scatter(df["Avg_Delay_Min"], df["Operating_Profit_INR"])
plt.title("Impact of Delays on Operating Profit")
plt.xlabel("Average Delay (Minutes)")
plt.ylabel("Operating Profit (INR)")
plt.show()

## Key Insights
- Routes with higher passenger load do not always generate the highest profits.
- Increased average delays are associated with lower operating profits.
- Certain routes demonstrate more stable profitability due to better operational efficiency.

## Conclusion & Recommendations
- IndiGo should prioritize reducing delays on high-traffic routes to protect margins.
- Route frequency should be optimized for consistently low-profit routes.
- Operational efficiency should be considered alongside load factor when evaluating performance.

